H4100.definition:
or מַה; or מָ; or מַ; also מֶה; a primitive particle;
properly, interrogative what? (including how? why? when?); but also exclamation, what! (including how!), or indefinitely what (including whatever, and even relatively, that which); often used with prefixes in various adverbial or conjunctive senses
KJV: how (long, oft, (-soever)), (no-) thing, what (end, good, purpose, thing), whereby(-fore, -in, -to, -with), (for) why.

H4101.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4100 (מָה)
{properly, interrogative what? (including how? why? when?); but also exclamation, what! (including how!), or indefinitely what}
KJV: how great (mighty), that which, what(-soever), why.

H4102.definition:
apparently a denominative from H4100 (מָה);
properly, to question or hesitate, i.e. (by implication) to be reluctant
KJV: delay, linger, stay selves, tarry.

H4103.definition:
from H1949 (הוּם);
confusion or uproar
KJV: destruction, discomfiture, trouble, tumult, vexation, vexed.

H4104.definition:
of Persian origin;
Mehuman, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV: Mehuman.

H4105.definition:
from H3190 (יָטַב) (augmented) and H410 (אֵל); bettered of God;
Mehetabel, the name of an Edomitish man and woman
KJV: Mehetabeel, Mehetabel.

H4106.definition:
or מָהִר; from H4116 (מָהַר);
quick; hence, skilful
KJV: diligent, hasty, ready.

H4107.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to cut down or reduce, i.e. by implication, to adulterate
KJV: mixed.

H4108.definition:
from H1980 (הָלַךְ);
a walking (plural collectively), i.e. access
KJV: place to walk.

H4109.definition:
from H1980 (הָלַךְ);
a walk, i.e. a passage or a distance
KJV: journey, walk.

H4111.definition:
from H4110 (מַהֲלָל) and H410 (אֵל); praise of God;
Mahalalel, the name of an antediluvian patriarch and of an Israelite
KJV: Mahalaleel.

H4112.definition:
from H1986 (הָלַם);
a blow
KJV: stripe, stroke.

H4113.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
perhaps an abyss
KJV: deep pit.

H4114.definition:
from H2015 (הָפַךְ);
a destruction
KJV: when...overthrew, overthrow(-n).

H4115.definition:
from H2015 (הָפַךְ);
a wrench, i.e. the stocks
KJV: prison, stocks.

H4116.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to be liquid or flow easily, i.e. (by implication); to hurry (in a good or a bad sense); often used (with another verb) adverbially, promptly
KJV: be carried headlong, fearful, (cause to make, in, make) haste(-n, -ily), (be) hasty, (fetch, make ready) [idiom] quickly, rash, [idiom] shortly, (be so) [idiom] soon, make speed, [idiom] speedily, [idiom] straightway, [idiom] suddenly, swift.

H4117.definition:
a primitive root (perhaps rather the same as H4116 (מָהַר) through the idea of readiness in assent);
to bargain (for a wife), i.e. to wed
KJV: endow, [idiom] surely.

H4118.definition:
from H4116 (מָהַר);
properly, hurrying; hence (adverbially) in ahurry
KJV: hasteth, hastily, at once, quickly, soon, speedily, suddenly.

H4119.definition:
from H4117 (מָהַר);
a price (for a wife)
KJV: dowry.

H4120.definition:
feminine of H4118 (מַהֵר);
properly, a hurry; hence (adverbially) promptly
KJV: hastily, quickly, shortly, soon, make (with) speed(-ily), swiftly.

H4121.definition:
from H4116 (מָהַר); hasty;
Maharai, an Israelite
KJV: Maharai.

H4122.definition:
from H4118 (מַהֵר) and H7998 (שָׁלָל) and H2363 (חוּשׁ) and H957 (בַּז); hasting (is he (the enemy) to the) booty, swift (to the) prey;
Maher-Shalal-Chash-Baz; the symbolical name of the son of Isaiah
KJV: Maher-sha-lal-bash-baz.

H4123.definition:
from H2048 (הָתַל);
a delusion
KJV: deceit.

H4124.definition:
from a prolonged form of the prepositional prefix m-and H1 (אָב); from (her (the mother's)) father;
Moab, an incestuous son of Lot; also his territory and descendants
KJV: Moab.

H4125.definition:
feminine מוֹאָבִיָּה; or מוֹאָבִיתxlit Môwâbîyth corrected to Môwʼâbîyth; patronymical from H4124 (מוֹאָב);
a Moabite or Moabitess, i.e. a descendant from Moab
KJV: (woman) of Moab, Moabite(-ish, -ss).

H4126.definition:
by transp. for H3996 (מָבוֹא);
an entrance
KJV: coming.

H4127.definition:
a primitive root;
to melt, i.e. literally (to soften, flow down, disappear), or figuratively (to fear, faint)
KJV: consume, dissolve, (be) faint(-hearted), melt (away), make soft.

H4128.definition:
a primitive root;
to shake
KJV: measure.

H4129.definition:
or rather מֹדָע; from H3045 (יָדַע);
an acquaintance
KJV: kinswoman.

H4131.definition:
a primitive root;
to waver; by implication, to slip, shake, fall
KJV: be carried, cast, be out of course, be fallen in decay, [idiom] exceedingly, fall(-ing down), be (re-) moved, be ready, shake, slide, slip.

H4132.definition:
from H4131 (מוֹט);
a wavering, i.e. fall; by implication, a pole (as shaking); hence, a yoke (as essentially a bent pole)
KJV: bar, be moved, staff, yoke.

H4133.definition:
feminine of H4132 (מוֹט);
a pole; by implication, an ox-bow; hence, a yoke (either literal or figurative)
KJV: bands, heavy, staves, yoke.

H4134.definition:
a primitive root;
to become thin, i.e. (figuratively) be impoverished
KJV: be (waxen) poor(-er).

H4135.definition:
a primitive root;
to cut short, i.e. curtail (specifically the prepuce, i.e. to circumcise); by implication, to blunt; figuratively, to destroy
KJV: circumcise(-ing), selves), cut down (in pieces), destroy, [idiom] must needs.

H4136.definition:
or מוֹל; (Deuteronomy 1:1), or מוֹאל; (Nehemiah 12:38), or מֻל; (Numbers 22:5), from H4135 (מוּל);
properly, abrupt, i.e. a precipice; by implication, the front; used only adverbially (with prepositional prefix) opposite
KJV: (over) against, before, (fore-) front, from, (God-) ward, toward, with.

H4137.definition:
from H3205 (יָלַד); birth;
Moladah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Moladah.

H4138.definition:
from H3205 (יָלַד);
nativity (plural birth-place); by implication, lineage, native country; also offspring, family
KJV: begotten, born, issue, kindred, native(-ity).

H4140.definition:
from H3205 (יָלַד); genitor;
Molid, an Israelite
KJV: Molid.

H4141.definition:
from H5437 (סָבַב);
a turn, i.e. circuit (of a building)
KJV: winding about.

H4142.definition:
or מֻסַבָּה; feminine of H4141 (מוּסָב);
a reversal, i.e. the backside (of a gem), fold (of a double-leaved door), transmutation (of a name)
KJV: being changed, inclosed, be set, turning.

H4143.definition:
from H3245 (יָסַד);
a foundation
KJV: foundation.

H4144.definition:
from H3245 (יָסַד);
a foundation
KJV: foundation.

H4145.definition:
feminine of H4143 (מוּסָד);
a foundation; figuratively, an appointment
KJV: foundation, grounded. Compare H4328 (מְיֻסָּדָה).

H4146.definition:
or מֹסָדָה; feminine of H4144 (מוֹסָד);
a foundation
KJV: foundation.

H4147.definition:
also (in plural) feminine מוֹסֵרָה; or מֹסְרָה; from H3256 (יָסַר);
properly, chastisement, i.e. (by implication) a halter; figuratively, restraint
KJV: band, bond.

H4148.definition:
from H3256 (יָסַר);
properly, chastisement; figuratively, reproof, warning or instruction; also restraint
KJV: bond, chastening(-eth), chastisement, check, correction, discipline, doctrine, instruction, rebuke.

H4149.definition:
or (plural) מֹסְרוֹת feminine of H4147 (מוֹסֵר); correction or corrections;
Moserah or Moseroth, a place in the Desert
KJV: Mosera, Moseroth.

H4150.definition:
or מֹעֵד; or (feminine) מוֹעָדָה; (2 Chronicles 8:13), from H3259 (יָעַד);
properly, an appointment, i.e. a fixed time or season; specifically, a festival; conventionally ayear; by implication, an assembly (as convened for a definite purpose); technically the congregation; by extension, the place of meeting; also a signal (as appointed beforehand)
KJV: appointed (sign, time), (place of, solemn) assembly, congregation, (set, solemn) feast, (appointed, due) season, solemn(-ity), synogogue, (set) time (appointed).

H4151.definition:
from H3259 (יָעַד); (as in H4150 (מוֹעֵד));
properly, an assembly  figuratively, a troop
KJV: appointed time.

H4152.definition:
from H3259 (יָעַד);
an appointed place, i.e. asylum
KJV: appointed.

H4153.definition:
from H4151 (מוֹעָד) and H3050 (יָהּ); assembly of Jah;
Moadjah, an Israelite
KJV: Moadiah. Compare H4573 (מַעֲדְיָה).

H4154.definition:
feminine passive participle of H4571 (מָעַד);
properly, made to slip, i.e. dislocated
KJV: out of joint.

H4155.definition:
from H5774 (עוּף);
properly, covered, i.e. dark; abstractly, obscurity, i.e. distress
KJV: dimness.

H4156.definition:
from H3289 (יָעַץ);
a purpose
KJV: counsel, device.

H4157.definition:
from H5781 (עוּק);
pressure, i.e. (figuratively) distress
KJV: affliction.

H4158.definition:
(Jeremiah 48:21) or מֵיפַעַת; or מֵפַעַת; from H3313 (יָפַע); illuminative;
Mophaath or Mephaath, a place in Palestine
KJV: Mephaath.

H4159.definition:
or מֹפֵת; from H3302 (יָפָה) in the sense of conspicuousness;
a miracle; by implication, a token or omen
KJV: miracle, sign, wonder(-ed at).

H4160.definition:
a primitive root;
to press, i.e. (figuratively) to oppress
KJV: extortioner.

H4161.definition:
or מֹצָאxlit môtsâ corrected to môtsâʼ; from H3318 (יָצָא);
a going forth, i.e. (the act) an egress, or (the place) an exit; hence, a source or product; specifically, dawn, the rising of the sun (the East), exportation, utterance, a gate, a fountain, a mine, a meadow (as producing grass)
KJV: brought out, bud, that which came out, east, going forth, goings out, that which (thing that) is gone out, outgoing, proceeded out, spring, vein, (water-) course (springs).

H4162.definition:
the same as H4161 (מוֹצָא);
Motsa, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Moza.

H4164.definition:
or מוּצָק; from H3332 (יָצַק);
narrowness; figuratively, distress
KJV: anguish, is straitened, straitness.

H4165.definition:
from H5694 (עָגִיל);
properly, fusion, i.e. literally, a casting (of metal); figuratively, a mass (of clay)
KJV: casting, hardness.

H4166.definition:
or מֻצָקָה; from H3332 (יָצַק);
properly, something poured out, i.e. a casting (of metal); by implication, a tube (as cast)
KJV: when it was cast, pipe.

H4167.definition:
a primitive root;
to jeer, i.e. (intens.) blaspheme
KJV: be corrupt.

H4168.definition:
from H3344 (יָקַד);
a fire or fuel; abstractly, a conflagration
KJV: burning, hearth.

H4169.definition:
feminine of H4168 (מוֹקֵד);
fuel
KJV: burning.

H4170.definition:
or מֹקֵשׁ; from H3369 (יָקֹשׁ);
a noose (for catching animals) (literally or figuratively); by implication, a hook (for the nose)
KJV: be ensnared, gin, (is) snare(-d), trap.

H4171.definition:
a primitive root;
to alter; by implication, to barter, to dispose of
KJV: [idiom] at all, (ex-) change, remove.

H4172.definition:
or מֹרָא; or מוֹרָהxlit môrâh corrected to môwrâh; (Psalm 9:20), from H3372 (יָרֵא);
fear; by implication, a fearful thing or deed
KJV: dread, (that ought to be) fear(-ed), terribleness, terror.

H4173.definition:
or מֹרַג; from an unused root meaning to triturate;
a threshing sledge
KJV: threshing instrument.

H4174.definition:
from H3381 (יָרַד);
a descent; as architecture, an ornamental appendage, perhaps a festoon
KJV: going down, steep place, thin work.

H4175.definition:
from H3384 (יָרָה); (see H3138 (יוֹרֶה))
an archer; also teacher or teaching; also the early rain
KJV: (early) rain.

H4176.definition:
or מֹרֶה; the same as H4175 (מוֹרֶה);
Moreh, a Canaanite; also a hill (perhaps named from him)
KJV: Moreh.

H4177.definition:
from H4171 (מוּר) in the sense of shearing;
a razor
KJV: razor.

H4178.definition:
from H3399 (יָרַט);
obstinate, i.e. independent
KJV: peeled.

H4179.definition:
or מֹרִיָּה; from H7200 (רָאָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); seen of Jah;
Morijah, a hill in Palestine
KJV: Moriah.

H4180.definition:
from H3423 (יָרַשׁ);
a possession; figuratively, delight
KJV: possession, thought.

H4181.definition:
feminine of H4180 (מוֹרָשׁ);
a possession
KJV: heritage, inheritance, possession.

H4182.definition:
from H3423 (יָרַשׁ) and H1661 (גַּת); possession of Gath;
Moresheth-Gath, a place in Palestine
KJV: Moresheth-gath.

H4183.definition:
patrial from H4182 (מוֹרֶשֶׁת גַּת);
a Morashtite or inhabitant of Moresheth-Gath
KJV: Morashthite.

H4184.definition:
a primitive root;
to touch
KJV: feel, handle.

H4185.definition:
a primitive root (perhaps rather the same as H4184 (מוּשׁ) through the idea of receding by contact);
to withdraw (both literally and figuratively, whether intransitive or transitive)
KJV: cease, depart, go back, remove, take away.

H4186.definition:
or מֹשָׁב; from H3427 (יָשַׁב);
a seat; figuratively, a site; abstractly, a session; by extension an abode (the place or the time); by implication, population
KJV: assembly, dwell in, dwelling(-place), wherein (that) dwelt (in), inhabited place, seat, sitting, situation, sojourning.

H4187.definition:
or מֻשִּׁי; from H4184 (מוּשׁ); sensitive;
Mushi, a Levite
KJV: Mushi.

H4188.definition:
patronymical from H4187 (מוּשִׁי);
a Mushite (collectively) or descendants of Mushi
KJV: Mushites.

H4189.definition:
act participle feminine of H4900 (מָשַׁךְ);
something drawing, i.e. (figuratively) a cord
KJV: band.

H4191.definition:
a primitive root;
to die (literally or figuratively); causatively, to kill
KJV: [idiom] at all, [idiom] crying, (be) dead (body, man, one), (put to, worthy of) death, destroy(-er), (cause to, be like to, must) die, kill, necro(-mancer), [idiom] must needs, slay, [idiom] surely, [idiom] very suddenly, [idiom] in (no) wise.

H4192.definition:
(Psalm H48 (אֲבִירָם) or מוּת לַבֵּן; from H4191 (מוּת) and H1121 (בֵּן) with the preposition and article interposed;
'To die for the son', probably the title of a popular song
KJV: death, Muthlabben.

H4193.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4194 (מָוֶת);
death
KJV: death.

H4194.definition:
from H4191 (מוּת);
death (natural or violent); concretely, the dead, their place or state (hades); figuratively, pestilence, ruin
KJV: (be) dead(-ly), death, die(-d).

H4195.definition:
from H3498 (יָתַר);
literally gain; figuratively, superiority
KJV: plenteousness, preeminence, profit.

H4196.definition:
from H2076 (זָבַח);
an altar
KJV: altar.

H4197.definition:
from an unused root meaning to mingle (water with wine);
tempered wine
KJV: liquor.

H4198.definition:
from an unused root meaning to suck out;
exhausted
KJV: burnt.

H4199.definition:
probably from an unused root meaning to faint with fear; terror;
Mizzah, an Edomite
KJV: Mizzah.
